  "worked_solution": "A biconditional expression $P\u21d4Q\u2261(P\u21d2Q)\u2227(Q\u21d2P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A\u21d4B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $3\\,|\\,x$ if and only if $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\n- $3\\,|\\,x$ is equivalent to $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\n- If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ and if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
